{"args":["object","get","POL-AGENT-INSTRUCTION-RUBRIC-001","--format","json","--context","mcp"],"body":"# Agent instruction processing rubric (kernel SSOT)\n\nCursor `.mdc` files are **projections**. This policy is the source of truth.\n\n## Requirement\nEvery agent response to a human (or directed peer) ask MUST execute these seven steps, in order, before claiming the ask is processed:\n\n1. **Frame** — Restate the ask in one sentence. Name success (what counts as an answer) and who/what is in scope.\n2. **Scope** — Classify: kernel object / code / ops / opinion. Name object ids (`BLI-*`, `PRI-*`, `POL-*`) or paths, or state none yet. Do not invent a new mission.\n3. **Observe** — Evidence from **this turn** (CLI output, log path, git SHA, `zqk object get`). State what is missing. Memory and prior chat are not evidence.\n4. **Hypothesize** — One claim. What would refute it. Comply with process-data CLI-only and never `git clean`/`restore` `docs/process/` instance YAML.\n5. **Test** — Smallest command **before** narrative. State success/fail criterion first.\n6. **Bound** — Timeout, load, what was **not** verified. “Not verified” is allowed. Do not assert scheduler/network without a command this turn.\n7. **Answer** — Lead with the answer, then evidence, then a follow-up id (`TRACK:` / BLI) or “permanent / no debt.”\n\n## Not the same as VDS\nVDS (`POL-WORKFLOW-VDS`) is the **done-gate** for BLI/CVS/CAP close. This rubric is **how to process an instruction** (investigate, metrics, opinion, implement, TPM duty). Both apply; neither substitutes for the other.\n\n## Mapping\n- Journalism 5W + how → Frame, Scope, Answer\n- Scientific method → Observe, Hypothesize, Test, Answer\n- Glossary: instruction processing rubric (link `glossary_term` created with this policy)\n- OHTV Cursor rule is the investigate/reliability **slice** of steps 3–6, not a second SSOT\n\n## Vendor projection\nProject to Cursor/IDE via `.cursor/rules/instruction-processing-rubric.mdc` citing **this policy id**. Do not treat `.mdc` as SSOT (`kernel vs IDE`).\n\n## Verify\n- This object `status=active`\n- Agent replies to mixed ask types show all seven steps (human spot-check)\n- `zqk object get POL-AGENT-INSTRUCTION-RUBRIC-001` (or the minted id) returns this body","category":"agent_guidance","command":"object get","context":"kernel-first instruction spine; Cursor rules are projections","created_at":"2026-08-18T05:48:48Z","created_by":"ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0","id":"POL-AGENT-INSTRUCTION-RUBRIC-001","kind":"policy","namespace_id":"zqk:kernel","policy_type":"requirement","priority_tier":"P0","related_object_refs":["GLS-1787032137731703000-65a92c1d","POL-WORKFLOW-VDS"],"schema_version":"2.0.0","status":"active","success":true,"title":"Agent instruction processing rubric","updated_at":"2026-08-18T05:49:15Z","updated_by":"ACC-1785920548450214012-68b850c0","version_context":"default"}

